/E (where the piece earns its headline. It concedes the real cost \(reform is slow; an officer moved every nine months starts things others quietly unwind\) before turning it. This honesty is what makes the closing line land rather than read as flattery. One thing to flag: I've kept "Domino's" unnamed in the body  described as the country's largest pizza chain. Named brands in an enforcement context invite legal correspondence you don't need. Blinkit, Zepto and Instamart are named, because those suspensions are on the public record via PTI and naming them is central to the point. If you want the pizza chain named too, it's defensible  your call, but I'd leave it. He cleared the MPSC in 2001, after three unsuccessful attempts. Three years later he)
